<title>BRAZIL: Brazil's Cia. Suzano year net lower.</title>
<headline>Brazil's Cia. Suzano year net lower.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazilian pulp and paper maker Cia. Suzano issued the following statement on its final 1996 results for its holding company:</p>
<p>		     1996			    1995</p>
<p>    shr	   27.48 reais		   368.17 reais</p>
<p>    net	   6.3 million			 84.8 million</p>
<p>    net revs    487.2 million		     542.9 million</p>
<p>NOTE: All figures in Brazilian reais.</p>
<p>Share profit figures are per 1,000 shares.  </p>
<p>Under the inflation-adjusted accounting method, Suzano reported net earnings of 17 million reais for 1996 vs 82.6 million.</p>
<p>The firm said its earnings were hurt by falling demand and prices in the international pulp and paper market, which, due to globalization, affected the country's domestic market.</p>
<p>((-- Romina Nicaretta, Sao Paulo Newsroom 5511 248 5415))</p>
